      <!-- Feature attributes (informative - ISO 19115 contentInfo does not itself carry per-attribute definitions; see ISO 19110 for a full feature catalogue): unit_id (BIGINT): A deterministic hash of a subset of the unit's own classification attributes (used to identify/dissolve H3 cells sharing the same classification result). Used as the GeoPackage feature id, but is not a persistently-assigned or guaranteed-unique per-feature identifier, and is not stable across reclassification runs if the hashed attributes change.; lu_code_primary (INTEGER): Primary (top-level, 1 digit) NZSLUC land use code, e.g. 1 = Conservation and natural environments, 2 = Production land uses, 3 = Built environments.; lu_code_secondary (INTEGER): Secondary (second-level) NZSLUC land use code, refining the primary code.; lu_code_tertiary (INTEGER): Tertiary (third-level, most specific) NZSLUC land use code, refining the secondary code.; lu_code (TEXT): Dotted concatenation of the primary, secondary, and tertiary codes (e.g. '1.3.6').; lu_description (TEXT): Human-readable label for the lu_code, derived from the NZSLUC v0.4.0 classification system definition.; lu_code_ancillary (TEXT): Additional/ancillary land use code(s) applicable to the same unit, where more than one use co-occurs.; commod (TEXT): Commodity or commodities associated with the classified use (e.g. specific crop or livestock types), where known.; manage (TEXT): Management practice(s) associated with the classified use (e.g. crop-pasture rotation, irrigation type), where known.; land_estate (TEXT): Estate/tenure type of the underlying property title (from LINZ District Valuation Roll / Records of Title), where available.; land_status (TEXT): Land governance/management status (e.g. Crown, local authority, private), derived primarily from the Central Record of State Land (CRoSL) and District Valuation Roll.; water (TEXT): Water feature type intersecting or coincident with the unit (e.g. river, lake, lagoon, swamp, mangrove), where applicable.; zone (TEXT): Planning zone category (e.g. Rural, Residential, Industrial, Commercial, Recreational), derived from District Valuation Roll zone codes.; confidence (INTEGER): Relative confidence in the classification of this unit (lower value = higher confidence), used to prioritise between competing candidate classifications during processing.; luc_date (DATE): Date on which this unit was processed/classified by the LUIS workflow.; source_data (TEXT): Name(s) of the contributing source dataset(s) that determined this unit's classification.; source_date (DATERANGE): Date range over which the contributing source data is valid/current.; source_scale (INT4RANGE): Spatial scale/precision range (in metres) of the contributing source data.; comment (TEXT): Free-text remarks; reserved for classification-specific notes. -->
