      <mdq:lineage>
        <mrl:LI_Lineage>
          <mrl:statement>
            <gco:CharacterString>NZLUM is produced by the Land Use Information System (LUIS), which partitions New Zealand's territorial sea extent into H3 discrete global grid cells at resolution 11, then evaluates each cell independently against a series of per-class rules drawing on a large and evolving set of authoritative input datasets. Where more than one candidate classification applies to a cell, rules prefer the more confident, more recent, and more spatially precise identification. Contributing input dataset categories include: Toitu Te Whenua Land Information New Zealand (LINZ) topographic, cadastral, and property/title datasets; Manaaki Whenua - Landcare Research datasets including the Land Cover Database (LCDB) and NZ Land Resource Inventory Land Use Capability (NZLRI LUC); Ministry for the Environment (MfE) and Statistics New Zealand (Stats NZ) datasets; Ministry for Primary Industries (MPI) marine farm data; and regional council resource-consent, contaminated-land (HAIL), land-categorisation, and land-use survey datasets from a wide range of regional and unitary authorities. The full, current list of contributing datasets changes as datasets are added and is intentionally not duplicated verbatim in this metadata record.</gco:CharacterString>
          </mrl:statement>
        </mrl:LI_Lineage>
      </mdq:lineage>
    </mdq:DQ_DataQuality>
  </mdb:dataQualityInfo>
